HOUSEHOLD INCOME
The Cheyenne service area’s median household income (MHI) is currently $59,994, which is slightly lower than the
county’s ($61,858) and state’s median ($65,783) (Figure 12). The household income is estimated to increase over the
next five years, bringing the MHI to $65,745 by 2028. The growth percentage is slightly lower than Wyoming’s household
income growth at 9.59%. Looking at the distribution of household income, 72% of residents in the service area make
less than $100,000, and 28% make less than $35,000 (Figure 13).
