Section II – Participation Figures

Participation Numbers: On an annual basis, the National Sporting Goods Association (NSGA)
conducts an in-depth study and survey of how Americans spend their leisure time. The data is
collected in one year and the report is issued in May of the following year.  This information
provides the data necessary to overlay rate of participation onto the Primary and Secondary Areas
to determine market potential.

B*K takes the national average and combines that with participation percentages of the Primary
and Secondary Service Areas based upon age distribution, median income, region and National
number.  Those four percentages are then averaged together to create a unique participation
percentage for the service area.  This participation percentage, when applied to the population of
the Primary and Secondary Service Areas, then provides an idea of the market potential for indoor
and outdoor recreation.

