The ESRI Business Analyst Recreation Expenditures Report looks at the annual spending potential
for five categories: TV/Audio/Video, Entertainment/Recreation Fees and Admissions, Recreational
Vehicles and Fees, Sports, Recreation and Exercise Equipment, and Photographic Equipment and
Supplies (Table 3). Information about non recreation/outdoor interests are included for spending
comparison to those highlighted in yellow. In 2023, Cheyenne residents spent a total of
$29,642,655 on TV/Audio/Video, followed by $15,579,895 on Entertainment and Recreation Fees
and Admissions18F19. $6,370,501 was spent on Sports, Recreation and Exercise in Cheyenne. Table 3
shows the different detailed expenditures falling under each of the five categories contributing to
the total recreational expenditure by the residents of Cheyenne. Spending on membership fees for
social/recreation/health clubs is considerable ($210.08 on average and $6.1 million total) and
exercise equipment and gear, game tables ($77.11 on average and $2.2 million total) which is
relevant in consideration of the opportunities that Cheyenne recreation facilities provide.

